<BaseLayout title="About Yu Zhehao" active="about" locale="en" description="About Yu Zhehao, with interests in theoretical physics, mathematics and AI.">
  <div class="page-shell">
    <header class="page-heading">
      <p class="page-kicker">ABOUT / YU ZHEHAO</p>
      <h1 class="page-title">Let curiosity take structure.</h1>
      <p class="page-lead">I have a long-term interest in theoretical physics, mathematics and artificial intelligence, especially in how mathematical structures can illuminate fundamental physics.</p>
    </header>
    <section class="section-block prose">
      <h2>Research interests</h2>
      <p>My interests move between quantum field theory, geometry, number theory and scientific computation. I am particularly interested in Feynman integrals and periods: how graph topology gives rise to geometric structures, how those structures can be detected and classified, and how they return to physical quantities after renormalization.</p>
      <p>I am also interested in AI as a tool for serious scientific work: not merely generating conjectures, but helping construct verifiable derivations, reproducible experiments and independent computational certificates.</p>
      <h2>Research principles</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>Distinguish theorems, conditional results, numerical evidence, conjectures and open problems.</li>
        <li>Prefer checkable definitions, derivations, code and data sources.</li>
        <li>Let computation serve mathematical and physical questions rather than replace proof.</li>
        <li>Keep the research process open to failure, correction and versioned records.</li>
      </ul>
    </section>
    <section class="section-block feature-panel">
      <p class="page-kicker">CONTACT / COLLABORATION</p>
      <h2>Stay curious. Stay in touch.</h2>
      <p>Open to conversations about mathematics, physics, AI and scientific computing.</p>
      <a class="button button-primary" href="https://github.com/Ynotfound" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">GitHub ↗</a>
    </section>
  </div>
</BaseLayout>
